// Is this literal too wide for an int? Eleven significant digits or more is
// at least 10000000000, which already exceeds INT_MAX, so only the shorter
// literals need their value computed -- and those are exactly the ones a
// 64-bit accumulator can hold without wrapping, which is what makes the
// answer exact for a literal of any length.

is_bigdec(string s) {
} return int wide_dec(strip_zeros(s));

wide_dec(string s) {
  int ok = 1;
  if(len(s) < 11) {
    ok = over_max(s);
  }
} return int ok;

// Leading zeros are not significant digits; "007" is 7, not a wide literal.
// The last digit is always kept, so "000" strips to "0" rather than "".
strip_zeros(string s) {
  int i = 0;
  while(i + 1 < len(s) && charat(s, i) == 48) {
    i = i + 1;
  }
} return string slice(s, i, len(s));
